{"cuisine/cuisine-of-new-york-city":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-new-york-city","n":"Cuisine of New York City","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine of the Mid-Atlantic United States","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-mid-atlantic-united-states"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["The cuisine of New York City consists of many cuisines that have been imported by immigrant communities. Almost all ethnic cuisines are present in New York."],["The city's New York Restaurant Week started in 1992 and has spread due to the discounted prices that are offered. New York hosts over 12,000 bodegas, delis, and groceries that supply those who enjoy these cuisines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-new-york-city"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_New_York_City"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Cuisine of the Mid-Atlantic United States","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-mid-atlantic-united-states"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Eat NYC: The Iconic Recipes That Feed the City","ref":"cookbook/eat-nyc-the-iconic-recipes-that-feed-the-city","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Yasmin Newman","note":"Home versions of well-known New York City dishes from bagels to street food.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781922754233","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Pizza in New York City","dish/pizza-in-new-york-city"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Cuisine of the Mid-Atlantic United States","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-mid-atlantic-united-states"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ed/Paulie_Gee%27s_Slice_Shop_%2835386%29.jpg/500px-Paulie_Gee%27s_Slice_Shop_%2835386%29.jpg","w":500,"h":397,"by":"Rhododendrites","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paulie_Gee's_Slice_Shop_(35386).jpg","of":"Pizza in New York City"}},"cuisine/henan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/henan-cuisine","n":"Henan cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Henan cuisine or Yu cuisine refers to the cooking styles of the Henan province in China. Being landlocked on all sides, the influence of localized culinary styles is plentiful in Henan cuisine, such as blending styles from Jiangsu and Beijing. Henan cuisine is known for its taste variety, including a blend of sour, sweet, bitter, spicy and salty. There are a wide variety of Henan dishes, including carp with fried noodles in sweet and sour sauce, grilled head and tail of black carp, Bianjing roasted duck, stewed noodles with mutton, and spicy soup. Henan cuisine is known for inducing a very moderate and balanced mix of flavours in its dishes, and has one of China's oldest and most traditional cooking styles."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"henan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Madame Huang's Kitchen: Henan cuisine","ref":"site/carolynjphillips-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"carolynjphillips.blogspot.com","note":"Recipe posts on Henan dishes from Carolyn Phillips' blog, Madame Huang's Kitchen.","url":"https://carolynjphillips.blogspot.com/search/label/Henan%20cuisine","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"All Under Heaven: Recipes from the 35 Cuisines of China","ref":"cookbook/all-under-heaven-recipes-from-the-35-cuisines-of-china","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Carolyn Phillips, 2016","note":"Regional survey of Chinese cooking that includes a section on Henan dishes.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/534780/all-under-heaven-by-carolyn-phillips/9781607749820/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c2/%E6%B2%B3%E5%8D%97%E6%BB%8B%E8%A1%A5%E7%83%A9%E9%9D%A2_3.jpg/500px-%E6%B2%B3%E5%8D%97%E6%BB%8B%E8%A1%A5%E7%83%A9%E9%9D%A2_3.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Mx. Granger","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B2%B3%E5%8D%97%E6%BB%8B%E8%A1%A5%E7%83%A9%E9%9D%A2_3.jpg"}},"cuisine/saraiki-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/saraiki-cuisine","n":"Saraiki cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Saraiki cuisine refers to the native cuisine of the Saraiki people in South Punjab. It is one of the key parts of the Pakistani and South Asian cuisines. Saraiki food comprises many unique local dishes, and also shares influences with neighbouring regional cuisines. The cities of Multan and Tonsa are the two main hubs of Saraiki cooking."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"saraiki-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saraiki_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"cuisine/andalusian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/andalusian-cuisine","n":"Andalusian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Spain","intro":[["Andalusian cuisine is the regional cuisine of Andalusia, Spain.  Notable dishes include gazpacho, fried fish (often called pescaíto frito in the local vernacular), the jamones of Jabugo, Valle de los Pedroches and Trevélez, and the wines of Jerez, particularly sherry. Culinary influences come from the historic Christian, Muslim, and Jewish traditions of the region. The oldest known cookbook of Andalusian cuisine, Kitab al tabij fi-l-Maghrib wa-l-Andalus fi `asr al-Muwahhidin, li-mu'allif mayhul, dates from the 13th century."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"andalusian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andalusian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Andalusia: Recipes from Seville and Beyond","ref":"cookbook/andalusia-recipes-from-seville-and-beyond","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"José Pizarro, 2019","note":"Spanish chef's collection of Andalusian dishes, published by Hardie Grant.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Andaluz: A Food Journey Through Southern Spain","ref":"cookbook/andaluz-a-food-journey-through-southern-spain","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Fiona Dunlop","note":"Recipes and food culture of Andalusia, published by Interlink.","url":"https://www.simonandschuster.ca/books/Andaluz/Fiona-Dunlop/9781623717285","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":8,"links":[["Ajoblanco","dish/ajoblanco"],["Chicharrón","dish/chicharron"],["Gachas","dish/gachas"],["Gazpachuelo","dish/gazpachuelo"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Porra antequerana","dish/porra-antequerana"],["Puchero","dish/puchero"],["Tocino de cielo","dish/tocino-de-cielo"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Pork belly","ingredient/pork-belly"],["Pork rind","ingredient/pork-rind"],["Lathyrus sativus","ingredient/lathyrus-sativus"],["Maize","ingredient/maize"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Fish stock","ingredient/fish-stock"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Pasta","ingredient/pasta"],["Potato","ingredie