"ingredient/ground-turkey","n":"Ground turkey","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Ground turkey, also known as turkey mince or minced turkey, is a mixture of dark and light turkey meat with remaining skin and visible fat processed together and minced until a \"ground\" form emerges. The turkey meat, skin, and fat is taken off the bone and processed with additives.  The final product has specific characteristics that appeal to customers, including a non pink color and non crumbly texture. The composition of ground turkey is driven by market demand, availability, and meat prices. The majority of ground turkey is made from excess thighs and drumsticks rather than the more costly breast meat. Ground turkey is a common low-fat alternative for ground beef."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ground-turkey"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ground_turkey"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine",[["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chickpea flour","ingredient/chickpea-flour"],["Dried lime","ingredient/dried-lime"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Meatball","ingredient/meatball"],["Onions","ingredient/onions"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9a/Cacatfood4_%285717210230%29.jpg/500px-Cacatfood4_%285717210230%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"pathwithpaws from Seattle, USA","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cacatfood4_(5717210230).jpg"}},"ingredient/pearl-barley":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pearl-barley","n":"Pearl barley","c":